      "message": "iterating through a SELECT and running an UPDATE for every row should really be in a transaction:\n\n    with migrate_engine.begin() as conn:\n        for user in conn.execute(sel):\n            values \u003d {\u0027domain_id\u0027: user[\u0027domain_id\u0027]}\n            stmt \u003d user_table.update().where(\n                user_table.c.id \u003d\u003d user[\u0027id\u0027]).values(values)\n            conn.execute(stmt)\n\nbut also, how many rows are we talking about for this table?   doing an UPDATE for every row in a SELECT suggests a single UPDATE that could do the whole thing with a correlated SELECT, should be much faster:\n\n    UPDATE user_table SET domain_id\u003d\n    (SELECT domain_id FROM child_user_table WHERE user_id\u003duser_table.id)\n    WHERE user_table.domain_id IS NULL",
